WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.410
All right, welcome to the program.

00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:03.499
Much to discuss, so let's get right into it.

00:00:03.499 --> 00:00:06.790
Donald Trump is starting to lose support with
white voters.

00:00:06.790 --> 00:00:12.570
This is the one demographic group that at
least until recently, Donald Trump still had

00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:13.570
supporting him.

00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:18.010
We looked at a cross-section of polling a
couple of weeks ago and we saw Joe Biden is

00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:19.980
winning the black vote.

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:22.500
Joe Biden is winning the Latino vote.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:24.300
Joe Biden is winning women.

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:26.410
Joe Biden is winning the college educated.

00:00:26.410 --> 00:00:28.330
However you want to slice and dice it.

00:00:28.330 --> 00:00:34.360
Donald Trump's resistance line demographically
was white voters, particularly white men,

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:37.720
particularly uneducated white voters.

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:41.770
But unfortunately for Trump, good for the
world.

00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:46.910
Donald Trump has lost some ground with white
voters relative to 2016.

00:00:46.910 --> 00:00:48.300
And it could be could.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:49.300
Right.

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:50.300
Depends on who votes.

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:52.290
Depends on whether votes are counted properly.

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:54.990
This could be Trump's undoing in November.

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:58.470
Let's look at some numbers in 2016.

00:00:58.470 --> 00:01:02.700
Donald Trump won white voters in Minnesota
by seven.

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:07.510
And right now, Trump is losing white voters
in Minnesota by two.

00:01:07.510 --> 00:01:14.620
That's a nine point swing against Trump among
Minnesota white voters.

00:01:14.620 --> 00:01:23.490
In Wisconsin, Trump won uneducated white women
by 16 in the last election, and he's now losing

00:01:23.490 --> 00:01:25.800
uneducated white women by nine.

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:32.550
That's a 25 point swing against Donald Trump
in Pennsylvania, where we have a lot of data

00:01:32.550 --> 00:01:33.550
on this.

00:01:33.550 --> 00:01:36.750
Biden and Trump are tied among white voters.

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:39.800
Trump won white voters in Pennsylvania in
2016.

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:45.850
But if you slice it down even further, Donald
Trump is struggling with Pennsylvania suburban

00:01:45.850 --> 00:01:47.400
white voters.

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:49.100
And this has been a gradual shift.

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:54.610
First, it was the college educated white voters
that started to move away from Donald Trump.

00:01:54.610 --> 00:02:00.440
Now you're even seeing noncollege educated
white voters starting to move away from Donald

00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:01.440
Trump.

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:02.990
Now, to be fair and to be thorough.

00:02:02.990 --> 00:02:06.909
There are some other slices where Trump has
improved since 2016.

00:02:06.909 --> 00:02:15.420
So if you look at Pennsylvania suburban white
women, Trump's doing okay with them.

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:19.990
Voters who disliked both Trump and Hillary
in 2016.

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:21.440
Trump is doing okay with them.

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:25.200
But these are potentially significant problems
for Donald Trump.

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:30.599
Again, with a major caveat if everyone's votes
are counted.

00:02:30.599 --> 00:02:35.380
Now, what's fascinating about this is that
as white voters have moved away from Donald

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:39.720
Trump, Trump has been more and more aggressively
throwing out sort of like red meat for white

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:45.970
voters lately, talking about saving the suburbs,
which has very racially coded language.

00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:51.510
He's even lamented voters who have to live
around refugees and immigrants in various

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:52.510
parts of the country.

00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:53.510
He did that at a recent.

00:02:53.510 --> 00:02:57.710
I think it was Pennsylvania and North Carolina
rallies, if I recall correctly.

00:02:57.710 --> 00:03:02.840
But regardless, white voters slowly moving
away from Donald Trump.

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:06.260
Now, will it be enough to make a difference
in the final calculation?

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:07.280
We don't know.

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:13.560
We don't know the the strategies that Trump
has left to actually win are dwindling.

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:19.470
One such strategy that Trump was hoping for
was announce a vaccine in October.

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:26.680
And unfortunately for him, two days ago, the
federal drug administrate, the FDA said that

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:32.550
they are making putting in place stricter
guidelines to approve a vaccine via an emergency

00:03:32.550 --> 00:03:33.970
use authorization.

00:03:33.970 --> 00:03:35.200
That's bad for Trump.

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:39.930
He's unlikely to get whatever boost he might
have gotten from a vaccine announcement.

00:03:39.930 --> 00:03:45.239
Will Trump push for some emergency stimulus
checks right before the election?

00:03:45.239 --> 00:03:49.750
I don't know that he even as the time I really
don't, particularly with the Senate going

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:50.750
into recess.

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:52.770
And just what is it, about 21 days, really?

00:03:52.770 --> 00:03:54.069
Just three weeks.

00:03:54.069 --> 00:03:56.129
So I don't know what Trump can do.

00:03:56.129 --> 00:04:01.459
And my sense, particularly from Donald Trump's
recent refusal to commit to a peaceful transition

00:04:01.459 --> 00:04:08.270
of power if he loses from Donald Trump's recent
revelation that we got about a strategy to

00:04:08.270 --> 00:04:12.129
